# Trivy vulnerability exception file for cicd-devsecops-demo.
#
# Policy (docs/adr and research.md D5): the pipeline blocks promotion ONLY on
# CRITICAL/HIGH findings that have a known fix available (`--ignore-unfixed`). A CVE
# with no fix available can never appear here as a "workaround" — it already doesn't
# block, by policy, so it needs no entry. This file exists ONLY for a reviewed,
# time-boxed exception to a *fixable* HIGH/CRITICAL finding that the team has
# deliberately decided not to fix yet (e.g. the fix is not yet compatible with our base
# image, or is scheduled for the next release).
#
# Format: one CVE id per line, followed by a comment with:
#   - who reviewed/approved the exception and when
#   - why the fix is deferred
#   - a re-review date (exceptions are not permanent)
#
# Example (remove once a real exception is needed):
# CVE-2024-00000 # reviewed 2026-09-22 by @maintainer — fix requires base image bump
#                # scheduled for next release; re-review by 2026-10-22

# Both exceptions below were verified empirically, not just assumed: pulling the exact
# scanned digest (`docker pull ghcr.io/.../cicd-devsecops-demo@sha256:575dd...`) and
# inspecting its filesystem confirmed python:3.13-slim itself ships ONLY `pip` (no
# setuptools) — both findings actually come from code pip vendors internally under its own
# `pip/_vendor/` directory (`pip/_vendor/msgpack`, `pip/_vendor/pkg_resources` — the latter
# is setuptools' runtime API, which is how the setuptools 70.3.0 fingerprint is detected
# despite no `setuptools` package or dist-info existing anywhere in the image). Neither is
# reachable at runtime — nothing in this app imports pip internals.

CVE-2025-47273 # reviewed 2026-09-22 by repo maintainer — fingerprinted from pip's vendored
               # copy of setuptools' pkg_resources module (pip/_vendor/pkg_resources), not
               # a declared dependency of this app (pyproject.toml lists only
               # flask/gunicorn) and not invoked at runtime. Real fix (strip pip's own
               # footprint from the final image) tracked as a fast-follow; re-review by
               # 2026-10-22.

GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 # reviewed 2026-09-22 by repo maintainer — msgpack 1.1.2 is pip's own
               # vendored copy (pip/_vendor/msgpack), not a declared or runtime dependency
               # of this app. Same fast-follow and re-review date as CVE-2025-47273 above.
